  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "681f872a-6e8d-4a2b-8c10-b6bb33af0c82",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -560,
        720
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 832,
        "content": "## Score and route new leads from a form using AI with round-robin SDR assignment\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow receives new lead form submissions, applies local configuration and email-domain classification, then uses AI to score and summarize the lead. It parses the AI response, routes unscorable leads to a human-review Slack alert, and checks whether successfully scored leads are hot. Hot leads are assigned to SDRs in round-robin order and announced in Slack, while all scored outcomes are merged, saved to Notion, confirmed by Gmail, and logged in Google Sheets.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the webhook URL as the submission target for the lead form and ensure the incoming fields match the code and AI prompt expectations.\n- Add credentials for OpenAI, Slack, Notion, Gmail, and Google Sheets in n8n.\n- Update the Config and round-robin code nodes with your scoring thresholds, SDR list, Slack channels, Notion database fields, email template details, and target Google Sheet.\n- Verify that the Notion database and Google Sheet contain the columns/properties referenced by the workflow.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the AI scoring prompt, hot-lead threshold, domain classification rules, SDR rotation list, and notification message templates to match your sales process."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
